.TH QLEVER\-UI 1 "2026-03-30" "qlever-ui" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qlever\-ui \- QLever UI development server and Django management tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qlever\-ui dev
.RI [ port ]
.br
.B qlever\-ui manage
.RI [ django\-command
.IR [args\|.\|.\|.] ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qlever\-ui
is a Django web application providing a browser-based interface for the
QLever SPARQL engine.
This command starts a local development server or runs Django management
commands.
.PP
On first use in a directory,
.B qlever\-ui
initialises the instance automatically:
.IP \(bu 2
If
.I ./qleverui.sqlite3
is absent, a default database (containing a demo admin account) is
copied from
.IR /usr/share/qlever\-ui/qleverui.sqlite3 .
.IP \(bu
If
.I ./qlever\-ui.env
is absent, it is copied from
.I /usr/share/qlever\-ui/qlever\-ui.env.default
and the placeholder secret key is replaced with a securely generated
random value.
.PP
Configuration is always read from
.I ./qlever\-ui.env
in the current working directory, and
.B QLEVERUI_DATABASE_URL
is always overridden to point to
.I ./qleverui.sqlite3
in that same directory.
Run
.B qlever\-ui
from the directory where the instance files should live.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.BR "dev " [ port ]
Apply pending database migrations, then start the Django development
server on
.RI 0.0.0.0: port
(default:
.IR 8176 ).
The UI is reachable at
.IR http://localhost:8176/ " (or the chosen port)."
The default database ships with an admin account
.RB ( demo : demo );
change this password before exposing the instance to a network.
Not intended for production use.
.TP
.BI "manage " "[django\-command [args\|.\|.\|.]]"
Pass arguments directly to
.BR django\-admin .
Useful for database migrations, account management, data import/export,
and other maintenance tasks.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Variables are read from
.IR ./qlever\-ui.env .
.TP
.B QLEVERUI_SECRET_KEY
Django secret key.
Generated automatically on first use.
.TP
.B QLEVERUI_DEBUG
Enable Django debug mode.
Default:
.IR True .
.TP
.B QLEVERUI_ALLOWED_HOSTS
Comma-separated list of hostnames Django will serve.
Default:
.IR localhost .
.TP
.B QLEVERUI_CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS
Comma-separated list of trusted origins for CSRF protection.
Default:
.IR http://localhost .
.TP
.B QLEVERUI_DATABASE_URL
Database URL.
Always overridden at startup to use the local SQLite file; any value
set in
.I qlever\-ui.env
is ignored.
.TP
.B QLEVERUI_STATIC_ROOT
Directory from which static files are served.
Default:
.IR /usr/share/qlever\-ui/static .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./qlever\-ui.env
Per-instance configuration (current directory).
.TP
.I ./qleverui.sqlite3
Application database (current directory).
.TP
.I /usr/share/qlever\-ui/qlever\-ui.env.default
Default configuration template.
.TP
.I /usr/share/qlever\-ui/qleverui.sqlite3
Default database (copied on first use).
.SH EXAMPLES
Start a fresh instance:
.PP
.EX
mkdir my\-qlever && cd my\-qlever
qlever\-ui dev
.EE
.PP
The server is then available at
.IR http://localhost:8176/ .
.PP
Start on a custom port:
.PP
.EX
qlever\-ui dev 9000
.EE
Log in to the admin panel at
.I http://localhost:8176/admin
with username
.B demo
and password
.BR demo .
.PP
List all available management commands:
.PP
.EX
qlever\-ui manage help
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
General QLever documentation:
.I https://docs.qlever.dev
.PP
QLever UI configuration guide:
.I https://github.com/qlever\-dev/qlever\-ui/blob/master/docs/configure_qleverui.md
